# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# THE MOST IMPORTANT FILE IN THIS REPO.
#
# Everything about, belonging to, or specific to a user lives under vault/.
# Nothing else in this repository is theirs. That is the whole boundary, and it
# is what makes an update possible: the system outside vault/ can be replaced
# wholesale without touching a year of somebody's working life.
#
# The rule below is a PATTERN, not a list. That distinction is the entire
# lesson: this file used to carry eight rules with `!` carve-outs naming
# individual files, and the rule they carved out of had already swallowed two
# files that needed to ship -- each found only because somebody noticed a clone
# was broken. A list has to be maintained by hand and fails the moment somebody
# adds a file and does not think to update it.
#
# WHY README FILES ARE TRACKED, AND NOTHING ELSE IS
#
# A user who downloads this has to know where to put their CV without reading
# documentation first. So the folders ship, with a README in each explaining
# what belongs there. The READMEs are the system's words, not the user's.
#
# The exceptions name FIVE EXACT PATHS rather than a `**/README.md` pattern, and
# that is not a relapse into listing files. A pattern looked cleaner and was
# wrong: the agent writes README files inside vault folders as it works, and
# `!vault/**/README.md` silently made every one of them stageable by `git add
# -A`. This list only ever grows when the SYSTEM adds a folder -- never when the
# USER adds a file, which is the failure mode that matters.
#
# tools/tests/test_boundary.py asserts these five, the five the pre-commit hook
# allows, and the five actually tracked are the SAME FIVE. Three lists that must
# agree cannot drift apart quietly. If you want to add a sixth, that is usually
# the signal that something is in the wrong folder.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

vault/**
!vault/README.md
!vault/migration/
!vault/migration/README.md
!vault/secrets/
!vault/secrets/README.md
!vault/settings/
!vault/settings/README.md
!vault/sources/
!vault/sources/README.md

.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
